 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "From the provided passages, no single model is explicitly recommended for night-only SAR. All cited manuals describe loss-of-link/failsafe behavior (RTH, hover, or land) and risk-management guidance from the FAA, but night-specific performance (e.g., thermal imaging, infrared) is not covered. The Matrice 30T and 4T provide configurable loss-of-signal actions and RTH behaviors; Autel Evo Max 4N also documents signal-loss handling and reconnection. Given night operations, you should prioritize models with reliable loss-of-link behavior and vision system stability, while noting visibility constraints noted for low-light conditions in the M30T guidance. Consider testing several units under night conditions to validate performance before procurement.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "FAA guidance emphasizes established loss-of-control procedures and risk management prior to operations, which informs selecting a SAR-capable platform.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0227",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0228"
      ],
      "quote": "These definitions are used to assign the level of risk prior to consideration of risk mitigation effects.",
      "conditions": [
       "Night operations not specified in guidance"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C001",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
